## Cancellation Breakdown

**Customer cancellation reasons:**

| Reason | Share |
|--------|-------|
| Wrong Address | 22.5% |
| Driver Issues | 22.4% |
| Driver Not Moving | 22.2% |
| Change of Plans | 21.9% |
| App Issues | 11.0% |

**Driver cancellation reasons:**

| Reason | Share |
|--------|-------|
| Customer-Related Issues | 25.3% |
| Capacity / Overcrowding | 25.0% |
| Personal & Car Issues | 24.9% |
| Customer Behaviour | 24.8% |

Both sides exhibit near-uniform distributions across reasons. This is systemic friction, not isolated incidents — and it demands parallel fixes, not a single solution.

---

## Key Takeaways

| Area | Finding |
|---|---|
| **Supply** | ~11K "No Driver Found" events indicate a platform-wide shortage, not a zone or category issue |
| **Cancellations** | ~27K driver cancels split evenly across four causes — requires four parallel interventions |
| **Revenue** | Auto + Go Mini ≈ ₹2.33 Cr combined; eBike + UberXL ≈ ₹51 L |
| **Pricing** | Distance (r = 0.42) is the only meaningful fare predictor; vehicle type and surge matter more |
| **Demand** | 18:00 is peak hour; weekends generate ~50% more revenue than any weekday |
| **Payments** | UPI leads valid transactions; ~48K records remain unclassified |
| **Ratings** | Inflation is structural on both sides — a 4.0 rating is a warning, not a midpoint |

---

## Recommendations

**① Fix the cancellation system — not just the symptoms**
- Capture group size at booking to prevent overcrowding cancellations before they occur
- Introduce dynamic cancellation penalties to disincentivise selective ride rejection
- Build a driver wellness scheduling system to reduce personal and vehicle-related abandonment

**② Close the supply gap with precision**
- Map every "No Driver Found" event to its hour and zone; deploy targeted incentives exactly there
- Pre-position drivers in the 17:00–19:00 window using demand forecasting — do not rely on passive surge

**③ Capture the weekend premium properly**
- Activate weekend-specific driver bonus schemes to ensure supply scales with the ~50% demand spike
- Launch a Friday evening campaign — the most undercaptured demand window in the dataset

**④ Resolve data quality issues before expanding analysis**
- Reclassify ~48K "Not Applicable" payment records — payment analysis is unreliable until this is resolved
- Add sub-reasons to "Customer-Related" driver cancellations — the current label is too broad to act on
- Enrich future datasets with: surge multiplier, zone-level supply ratio, driver tenure, and vehicle age

**⑤ Invest in what works; review what doesn't**
- Auto and Go Mini are the revenue engine — protect supply, reduce cancellations, and strengthen incentives
- Uber Wallet is an underutilised loyalty lever — wallet users are the platform's highest-value repeat customers
- eBike and UberXL warrant a formal strategic review; they are not self-sustaining at current volumes

---

## Modelling Use Cases

This dataset is well-suited for the following downstream applications:

- **Cancellation Prediction** — classify pre-trip cancellation risk before a driver accepts
- **Revenue Forecasting** — time-series modelling of daily and weekly booking value
- **Supply–Demand Modelling** — map "No Driver Found" events to zone and hour for targeted intervention
- **Driver Segmentation** — cluster by cancellation rate, ratings, earnings, and vehicle type
- **Customer Segmentation** — segment by vehicle preference, payment method, and booking frequency
- **Surge Pricing Analysis** — model fare variance unexplained by distance to surface surge patterns
- **Rating System Research** — study bilateral rating behaviour and inflation at scale

